#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff04ceeb-c9f6-5562-b494-204eb62d7f5b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of the Points of Intersection of a Trigonometric Curve and a Horizontal Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3c3b7fa-7ec4-58a0-a5f6-2c752977ed30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294240} {:answer/id #uuid "8d621446-a4c1-5070-b626-77ed872c6c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294241} {:answer/id #uuid "df24ba6b-c0c0-53dc-ac84-f8a75abf42dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294242} {:answer/id #uuid "f5420b55-8b2c-5d50-8551-0c8f85248e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294243} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbeaf68-b5dd-5406-a2f6-7b2727e938af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d621446-a4c1-5070-b626-77ed872c6c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294241} :answer-field/id #uuid "918661ac-38f4-5659-b7bd-83f2c2390cde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4653a01e-6fa4-5345-8443-e064ea5e4a3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120789" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035241/assets/8197d1111bbd4c3b8908bc12cbc58561ffd23fe06d9f9fa99f9ab815ed78733f.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Which of the following generates the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035241/assets/ba34bf96662682ec433c3ade0bf3f118638212101a0729fe95bbae05aee8bf1e.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186258090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b12a7b7-1df3-5203-934e-8820604de3de" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c800bf1-db0e-5a4f-b1f7-79de46c24ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294266} {:answer/id #uuid "7bdc1a32-3ddc-5b62-b443-798708784e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294267} {:answer/id #uuid "8fbfce8f-1539-5097-be10-dbae597cac5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294268} {:answer/id #uuid "2ee8162a-22a0-5c9e-b9db-f9b656661d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294269} {:answer/id #uuid "976eda39-25fa-5c0c-ada1-63cab5aa0334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fbfce8f-1539-5097-be10-dbae597cac5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294268} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a0acda-284b-5a31-8855-d2a8a1ff7df1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4878f13e-2679-5b9e-8cae-9094f9bb2d55" :question/math-academy-id "q-141281" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column or Row of the Identity Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d130fa2-0493-59f0-af50-5160da776d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279077} {:answer/id #uuid "51168f06-2e01-5b0b-8693-e06b3de9dde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279078} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd472d0-73ef-50e9-855a-0399cfed9979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279079} {:answer/id #uuid "4460027c-0c38-5e6a-8d86-3dc9b9c03c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279080} {:answer/id #uuid "3d480acf-3659-5c9e-a0aa-59046b467d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4460027c-0c38-5e6a-8d86-3dc9b9c03c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279080} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5abea32-c0b7-548b-8c88-75fbbdda6178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7963c06-fa30-5a29-ac72-ec8ff733ff33" :question/math-academy-id "q-41944" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "831f9aa0-099e-5e0c-8a9d-c4828b629f64" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f10507d-8411-501b-bf2a-099f1599108a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294349} {:answer/id #uuid "6b40c74f-5636-54fa-8e48-1cc8dc48453b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294350} {:answer/id #uuid "a8890cb1-796d-5e73-9f8e-477954728915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294351} {:answer/id #uuid "f886e3e2-bc69-5e9f-8cd6-9f9f6b4e1c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294352} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9f71ba-6aae-578e-ae86-a1f2d811e951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b40c74f-5636-54fa-8e48-1cc8dc48453b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294350} :answer-field/id #uuid "0028443c-1e65-58fd-b318-c517c386e7d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8bb03c0c-2bf3-5dda-8102-58698d5cc17e" :question/math-academy-id "q-65502" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9921209-dae9-5088-9de7-05c7fd47e501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7-2\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294381} {:answer/id #uuid "3754d50a-db5d-5ff0-b7b6-372317e63a2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ -7+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294382} {:answer/id #uuid "c9681e1b-016c-5383-b6d6-a29ae4e874ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7-2\\text{i} \\\\ -1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294383} {:answer/id #uuid "bd707435-20e3-5699-af51-97510db3a9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1-2\\text{i} \\\\ 7-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294384} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb85375-392a-5d81-a298-78fb82c7fe13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 7+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd707435-20e3-5699-af51-97510db3a9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1-2\\text{i} \\\\ 7-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294384} :answer-field/id #uuid "79d7745d-f9d6-5352-a971-0ad567d7937d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93cd3e49-db0b-5ee5-918c-8c97827d57f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76209" :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}(1+2\\text{i})+(2-\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) \\\\ (1-2\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i})+2(1-\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\text{i}-2)+(1-3\\text{i}) \\\\ 5+(2-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-2\\text{i} \\\\ 7-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
